README.md:90:planning; explanation approval retains it through execution. Terminal coordinated review releases the matching lock. Interrupted locks require reconciliation and explicit resume.
README.md:125:An executor may return `{"kind":"needs_input","question":"...","recommendedAnswer":"...","affectedRequirement":"..."}`. Ralph persists the question on its run/issue/attempt and publishes it through the main-session adapter. The issue and descendants wait while independent issues continue. Human waiting consumes no executor capacity, agent deadline or retry. A correlated clarification resumes the same worktree and attempt with a new job identity and the remaining active-time budget.
README.md:127:Hosts answer through the adapter's authenticated `UserInputResult` contract. The public router also accepts a later response via `answerExecutorQuestion`, followed by `scheduleIssues` for clarification or `continuePlanning` for revision approval. Stale requests, changed revisions, duplicate messages and unrelated sessions are rejected. The production chat tool binds the actual user message to the pending request and revision; assistant-generated text cannot approve.
README.md:129:For scope changes, a correlated user answer can carry JSON `{"kind":"revise_scope","prd":"complete PRD text","graph":<complete graph>,"files":<issue-path to Markdown map>}`. Ralph compares content, validates and publishes a new draft, presents affected work and preserved integrated evidence, and requires the normal combined execution approval. Adapter-delivered answers present that gate automatically. Revised artifacts cannot execute under the previous approval. Answers and approvals have no browser mutation endpoint.
README.md:137:A completed agent job is not proof of a verified feature. Reports distinguish `verified`, `incomplete-validation` (including skipped checks), `unverified` (missing review evidence) and `unresolved` (blocking issues/findings). Inspect the report's commit, checks, unavailable review and cleanup/resource fields. No workflow script publishes, pushes, creates a PR or merges into a target branch.
README.md:144:bun test tests/e2e/full-workflow.test.ts
README.md:149:The package probe builds a clean distribution, packs it, installs it into two committed temporary repositories with spaces in their paths, and loads the installed plugin. It checks bundled skills/dashboard assets, separate stores and dashboard data, concurrent ports, argv preservation, local readiness, child cleanup and pause/resume. The workflow demo approves discovered commands, interviews, generates and approves a PRD/issue graph, prepares a clean baseline, executes real red/green addition tests, commits through the executor/merger worktrees, and dispatches independent reviewers through the fake SDK HTTP boundary. The second repository really times out its approved validation check; no execution state is seeded. The host explicitly supplies functional review options to the public coordinator after scheduling. Reports are `verified` for the passing-evidence fixture and `incomplete-validation` for the skipped-evidence fixture. These are deterministic fixture verdicts, not live-agent evidence. Temporary repositories are removed; `test:package` prints platform, runtime, outcomes and blockers. Set `PACKAGE_EVIDENCE_PATH` to retain JSON evidence.
README.md:151:For the real installed OpenCode server probe, enable `OPENCODE_SMOKE=1` (PowerShell: `$env:OPENCODE_SMOKE='1'`) before `bun run test:smoke`. It uses a local deterministic model. The separate credentialed session probe requires `OPENCODE_LIVE_SMOKE=1`, `OPENCODE_SMOKE_URL` and `OPENCODE_SMOKE_MODEL=provider/model`; without them it reports SKIPPED. The credentialed probe covers a model session, not the complete workflow; native interactive rendering and full live-workflow evidence remain separate verification requirements. A v2 server also requires authentication: set `OPENCODE_SMOKE_PASSWORD` for the live probe. Credentials remain in the configured server; do not copy them into fixtures or package assets.
README.md:157:All Ralph questions and approvals accept your normal reply in the current chat. `/ralph-answer` is no longer registered.

