docs/wiki/features/workflow-recovery.md:57:Question/approval persistence and executor/validation recovery have public-fixture coverage. Native feature input uses the host question tool; the obsolete chat transport and second execution approval have been deleted. The automatic review handoff reconstructs its approved lifecycle after explicit resume. Ambiguous publication, cleanup and repair operations stay blocked. Native Linux/Windows process trees and interactive live shutdown still require separate evidence.
docs/troubleshooting.md:30:Feature questions and scope approval use the host’s native question tool. Enable it and inspect `/ralph-status` for the pending request and owning stage. `/ralph-orchestrator` opens a fresh interview; accepted PRD completion opens a fresh planner. Execution progress and the report appear in the planner chat. Ordinary chat replies cannot approve a feature. Setup saving and removal still use chat approval. `ralph_workflow` and `/ralph-answer` are removed.
docs/opencode-compatibility.md:65:Ralph starts feature stages directly and uses native question forms for feature input and one scope authorization. The full grill-me skill runs in a fresh interview; create-prd runs in that session after approval; the full adapted to-issues skill runs in a fresh session. `ralph_complete_interview`, `ralph_complete_prd` and `ralph_complete_issues` validate owner/session/attempt and accepted artifacts. Issue completion starts execution automatically. Progress and results target the issue-planning chat. There is no chat reply transport or second execution approval. Setup saving and previewed removal retain ordinary-chat approvals.
README.md:129:For scope changes, use `ralph_request_product_decision` from the owning stage. Revised explanations require a newly displayed native scope authorization and invalidate dependent planning outputs. Executors that discover changed requirements return a correlated scope proposal with a revised explanation; accepted artifacts must be regenerated under renewed authorization. Integrated evidence is retained. There is no second graph or execution approval and no browser mutation endpoint.
